From 69d510cd262874165ee839f6fff1b0e898fa08df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sn3ro <zak.darek@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:26:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(machine): a laser machine kind and a laser head tool
 kind

Slice 1 of the laser profile cut (#4081): the two kinds that the
operation needs, and no operation or post yet.

- post::machine: Kind::Laser, declared only ("laser", "laser cutter",
  "laser cutting"): an X/Y gantry with an optional focus Z, no spindle,
  no live tool, no coolant and no rotary. The waterjet and laser doors
  share no_spindle::xy_gantry_refusals and Machine::xy_gantry_sane.
- tools: ToolKind::Laser, the laser head - diameter is the beam kerf,
  rpm 0, no corner radius, no cutting data rows (the operation will
  state the power and the feed). camcraft_tools::laser::laser_tool.
- app: the project file reads and writes the kind ("laser"); the editor
  validator and the blank draft know the kind; no family admits a laser,
  the create gate and the program check refuse each operation by name,
  and no built-in post serves a laser.
- ui: the kind in the machine editor, the tool tables and the panes; an
  original tool-laser glyph. The New Tool combo does not offer the laser
  head before an operation accepts it.

Refs #4081

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
